WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.990
Long ago, in a faraway village in Africa, there lived a famous blacksmith.

2
00:00:05.991 --> 00:00:08.054
His name was Kintae.

3
00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:14.431
Every morning, people would come to watch him work, and he liked having the people nearby.

4
00:00:14.432 --> 00:00:20.660
He would hammer the red-hot iron, and the people would sing to his steady beat.

5
00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:28.727
One morning a messenger from the king's court ran to Kintae's home and said, "The king wants to see you immediately.

6
00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.559
He has a job for you to do."

7
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.386
Kintae was very happy. He quickly got dressed and hurried to the palace.

8
00:00:36.387 --> 00:00:40.856
He passed many of his friends as he walked to the palace.

9
00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:44.794
To each of them he said proudly: "The king has sent for me!

10
00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:46.385
He has a job for me!"

11
00:00:46.386 --> 00:00:49.877
When Kintae reached the palace, he had to wait.

12
00:00:49.878 --> 00:00:54.036
While he waited, he wondered why the king had sent for him.

13
00:00:54.037 --> 00:01:02.346
Kintae often made things for the palace, but usually one of the king's servants told Kintae what to make.

14
00:01:02.347 --> 00:01:06.252
When Kintae saw the king, he bowed very low.

15
00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:10.591
"You may stand," said the king, and Kintae stood.

16
00:01:10.592 --> 00:01:16.984
"I have sent for you," continued the king, "because I have a special task for you."

17
00:01:16.985 --> 00:01:22.092
The king clapped his hands, and servants carried in baskets full of iron.

18
00:01:22.093 --> 00:01:25.819
They placed the baskets in front of Kintae.

19
00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:30.785
"You are to take this metal and make it into a man," said the king.

20
00:01:30.786 --> 00:01:36.983
"A real, living man who can walk, talk, think, and has blood in his veins."

21
00:01:36.984 --> 00:01:42.014
Kintae lowered his eyes because what the king asked was impossible.

22
00:01:42.015 --> 00:01:48.469
Kintae was also afraid because to say no to the king was the same as asking for death.

23
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:55.637
Kintae did not want to die, so he again bowed very low and said, "Yes, Your Majesty."

24
00:01:55.638 --> 00:02:02.906
The king's servants carried the iron back to Kintae's shop, but as he followed, he kept his eyes lowered.

25
00:02:02.907 --> 00:02:05.502
Kintae knew his days were numbered.

26
00:02:05.503 --> 00:02:11.020
He spent his days and nights looking for a solution to his problem.

27
00:02:11.021 --> 00:02:13.838
His friends made many suggestions.

28
00:02:13.839 --> 00:02:19.458
"Couldn't you make an iron shell, so a man could get inside it?" suggested one friend.

29
00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:27.491
Another friend said, "I think you should run away to a faraway country and start life all over again where no one knows you."

30
00:02:27.492 --> 00:02:31.012
His friends meant well, but they couldn't help Kintae.

31
00:02:31.013 --> 00:02:33.770
He was so worried he became sick.

32
00:02:33.771 --> 00:02:41.828
He couldn't eat, he couldn't sleep, and he couldn't work because he couldn't think about anything except the king's task.

33
00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:48.030
One evening, as he walked through a lonely area of the fields, he heard something strange.

34
00:02:48.031 --> 00:02:51.035
He went closer to find out what it was.

35
00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:56.647
As he got closer, he saw his boyhood friend singing to himself.

36
00:02:56.648 --> 00:03:01.020
Sadly, his old friend had gone mad a long time ago.

37
00:03:01.021 --> 00:03:04.251
He lived alone in the bush far from town.

38
00:03:04.252 --> 00:03:09.773
"Hi, Kintae," said his crazy boyhood friend. "Thank you for visiting me.

39
00:03:09.774 --> 00:03:14.237
I knew you were coming so I prepared this feast for us. Come, sit down."

40
00:03:14.238 --> 00:03:18.367
The meal wasn't really a feast, but it was delicious.

41
00:03:18.368 --> 00:03:25.061
They ate berries and some honey. Suddenly Kintae realized how hungry he was.

42
00:03:25.062 --> 00:03:29.264
This was the first food he had eaten in several days.

43
00:03:29.265 --> 00:03:35.275
The food made him feel better, and he began to tell his old friend about the king's task.

44
00:03:35.276 --> 00:03:39.404
"Well," finished Kintae, "that is my story."

45
00:03:39.405 --> 00:03:43.623
"I know what you must do," said his old friend immediately.

46
00:03:43.624 --> 00:03:48.640
"Go and tell the king that you need special ingredients for this task.

47
00:03:48.641 --> 00:03:55.512
Tell him you need one thousand carts of charcoal made from human hair, and one hundred buckets full of human tears."

48
00:03:55.513 --> 00:03:59.849
After his old friend said this, he laughed like a madman.

49
00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:04.915
Kintae thanked his friend for such good advice and then returned to the city.

50
00:04:04.916 --> 00:04:08.358
At first light, he hurried to the king's palace.

51
00:04:08.359 --> 00:04:15.164
When Kintae saw the king, he bowed low. "You may stand," said the king.

52
00:04:15.165 --> 00:04:19.865
"Why have you come? Is the man finished?" asked the king.

53
00:04:19.866 --> 00:04:22.543
Kintae said, "No, Your Majesty.

54
00:04:22.544 --> 00:04:25.556
I need special ingredients to complete your task."

55
00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:33.351
Kintae told the king what he needed, and the king ordered all his subjects to cut their hair and to cry into buckets.

56
00:04:33.352 --> 00:04:35.770
The people did their best.

57
00:04:35.771 --> 00:04:40.496
They shaved their heads and cried into their buckets, but it wasn't enough.

58
00:04:40.497 --> 00:04:45.378
Only two pots of tears and one load of charcoal were collected.

59
00:04:45.379 --> 00:04:49.330
When the king learned of these results, he sent for Kintae.

60
00:04:49.331 --> 00:04:53.592
Kintae was very afraid when he went back to the king.

61
00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:59.347
"Kintae," said the king, "you have asked me for something that is impossible.

62
00:04:59.348 --> 00:05:05.775
My people can never grow enough hair, nor cry enough tears to give you the ingredients you need.

63
00:05:05.776 --> 00:05:08.627
I therefore free you from your task."

64
00:05:08.628 --> 00:05:11.747
"Yes, Your Majesty," replied Kintae.

65
00:05:11.748 --> 00:05:16.965
As he walked away from the king, he took a breath.

66
00:05:16.966 --> 00:05:19.959
It felt like he hadn't breathed for weeks.

67
00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.231
He was happy again, and he smiled all the way home.

68
00:05:24.232 --> 00:05:30.086
As time went on, the king and his people forgot about Kintae's impossible task.

69
00:05:30.087 --> 00:05:33.556
But Kintae never forgot who had saved him.

70
00:05:33.557 --> 00:05:40.159
Kintae made sure that his old friend never felt hungry or thirsty again.

